From 3c2d490992928d271ad523c48f34d50798771c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:10:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Item grid widget for menus: the QIO Dashboard's catalogue
 (API 55)

A menu screen takes an item_grid widget (columns by rows of cells) showing
entries the mod gives: world.set-menu-grid for a block's menu (kept while
the game runs, sent on open), an item menu's menu-grid. Counts past 999 are
abbreviated (1.2k), the wheel and a bar scroll it, the hovered cell's
tooltip gives the item and its whole count. A press on a cell goes to the
mod's new export menu-grid-click with the entry, button, Shift and the
cursor stack; its answer sets the cursor and fills the inventory. Search is
the menu's text box. Example qio-demo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
